                <property name="title">
                 <string/>
                </property>
                <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="horizontalLayout_19">
                 <property name="leftMargin">
                  <number>3</number>
                 </property>
                 <property name="topMargin">
                  <number>3</number>
                 </property>
                 <property name="rightMargin">
                  <number>3</number>
                 </property>
                 <property name="bottomMargin">
                  <number>3</number>
                 </property>
                 <item>
                  <widget class="QRadioButton" name="freqDigitTypeCATRadioButton">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>Readable digits left to right, usually for CAT.
</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>NORMAL</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="checked">
                    <bool>true</bool>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item>
                  <widget class="QRadioButton" name="freqDigitTypeCIVRadioButton">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>ICOM CI-V reversed jumble of crap style</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>CI-V</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                 <item>
                  <widget class="QRadioButton" name="freqDigitTypeBCDRadioButton">
                   <property name="toolTip">
                    <string>FT-857(D) or FT-897 era radios</string>
                   </property>
                   <property name="text">
                    <string>BCD (old Yaesu)</string>
                   </property>
                  </widget>
                 </item>
                </layout>
               </widget>
              </item>
              <item row="5" column="0" colspan="2">
               <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="freqHelpTextEdit">
                <property name="readOnly">
                 <bool>true</bool>
                </property>
                <property name="plainText">
                 <string>VFO command prefix - for all radios, fill in VFO A.  CAT style radios usually have a separate command for setting VFO B, otherwise, leave it blanke.

Number of Frequency Digits - how many digits are required to be in the command.  Frequency is supplies in Hz, so front padding will be applied to ensure the command has this many &quot;digits&quot; of frequency information.

Command Suffix - the end of the command, such as &quot;FD&quot; in CI-V for ICOM, or &quot;;&quot; for CAT.  For OLD BCD type Yaesu's it will likely be &quot;01&quot; which is the command for setting the current VFO.

Order of Digits - 
&quot;NORMAL&quot; means for CAT, which is front zero padded in order of Hz.  
&quot;CI-V&quot; builds the ridiculous ICOM frequency format
&quot;BCD&quot; (old Yaesu) will designate normally sequenced digits, but sent in binary instead of text.</string>
                </property>
               </widget>
              </item>
             </layout>
            </widget>
           </item>
